& [Delineation]
  + the retained prefix is complete replay authority while the attention reentry frame is a compact derived transport view
  + a SHA-256 commitment detects changed retained inputs but does not reproduce their omitted semantic content for a model
  + structural surface equivalence means host-visible model quota tool schema phase latest call projection and final schema agree
  + structural surface equivalence is not model-output semantic equivalence provider compatibility or quality evidence
  + the compact request remains experimental and does not replace the authoritative full request

& [SelectedForms]
  + AttentionReentryFrame binds exact prefix identity through digest and current public head fields without registry or record body
  + compact messages retain the objective a serialized frame and only the last valid assistant tool-call plus matching tool projection
  + advance and reflect-terminal builders use separate system directives and preserve their distinct tool and response-schema surfaces
  + validators recompute full prefix frame compact request and tail correspondence from exact host-retained inputs
  + quota-one experiment measures every nonempty prefix until terminal and compares full with compact request sizes

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty keeps digest commitment structural equivalence and semantic equivalence claims distinct
  + Security binds frame to exact retained prefix head phase and latest call before constructing a request
  + Planner retains quota cap next operation and terminal tool disablement
  + Weaver composes objective frame latest call and projection while the host preserves full causal history
  + Scribe records commitment measurements and explicit nonclaims
  + Refiner removes older repeated call pairs from model-facing transport only
  + Observer compares reconstructed full and compact structural surfaces before admitting experiment evidence

